@spec cmgr_manifest_spec  src=tests/specs/cmgr_manifest_spec.lua  loc=239  cases=13

# Intent
  The manifest declares each command once, under the group it reads in, carrying
  its label and its keys as binding tokens. Pins that install parses those tokens
  into the declaring scope's keymap, stamps the group onto the entry, that a
  keyless entry binds nothing, that declaration order survives within a group,
  that a name declared twice raises, that a token which does not parse raises,
  that the surface is the reachable scopes' entries, and that the load-time audit
  raises in both directions, and on a scope that registers a command while
  declaring no manifest at all.

# Helpers
  @fn fresh()  @ 17
  @fn noop()  @ 19

# Cases
  @case 'install parses each entry\'s tokens into its own scope\'s keymap'  [pure]  @ 23-35
  @case 'install stamps the group onto each entry'  [pure]  @ 41-52
  @case 'an entry with no keys binds nothing'  [pure]  @ 56-62
  @case 'a group is a list, so declaration order survives install'  [pure]  @ 66-78
  @case 'the surface is the entries of the scopes on the stack'  [pure]  @ 84-99
  @case 'a modal scope drops what it does not pass through from the surface'  [pure]  @ 105-120
  @case 'a declared family shares a group and one mask over its bases'  [pure]  @ 128-158
  @case 'a token that does not parse raises, naming the command'  [pure]  @ 162-173
  @case 'a command declared by two scopes raises at install'  [pure]  @ 177-188
  @case 'audit is quiet when entries and registrations correspond'  [pure]  @ 192-202
  @case 'audit raises on a scope that registers but declares no manifest'  [pure]  @ 206-214
  @case 'audit raises on an entry no scope registers'  [pure]  @ 218-225
  @case 'audit raises on a registered command its scope does not declare'  [pure]  @ 229-237

